From 18cb09a4e1f229f6264cbdd2fc373c14676f7136 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mminin <mminin2010@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:45:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] XFA: Complete FormCalc's built-in functions

Add the FormCalc functions that were missing, following Adobe's FormCalc
reference: the financial functions Apr, CTerm, FV, IPmt, NPV, Pmt, PPmt,
PV, Rate and Term; the time functions Time2Num, Num2Time, Num2GMTime,
IsoTime2Num, TimeFmt and LocalTimeFmt; Format and Parse; WordNum,
UnitType, UnitValue, Eval, Null and Ref. Get, Post and Put throw, since
forms may not reach the network.

Date and time functions now use picture clauses and the form's locales,
so Date2Num and Num2Date take a locale and understand every date symbol,
DateFmt and LocalDateFmt give the locale's patterns, and Time() counts
milliseconds from midnight GMT as FormCalc specifies. Date2Num's default
format is now "MMM D, YYYY", as specified. Encode and Decode handle the
html and xml types.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
